nd transitional loans for real estate investors; and origination and sale of loans. The company provides structured multi-family property investments; other mortgage-, residential housing- and credit-related assets and strategic investments; and commercial mortgage-backed securities (CMBS). It generally would not be subject to federal corporate income taxes if it distributes at least 90% of its taxable income to its stockholders. Adamas Trust, Inc. was formerly known as New York Mortgage Trust, Inc. and changed its name to Adamas Trust, Inc. in September 2025. Adamas Trust, Inc. was incorporated in 2003 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason T. Serrano | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $4.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 221 people. Each employee generates $570K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Adamas Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $474M market cap.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $126M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.90\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 16.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 93% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Contrast: Adamas Trust (NASDAQ:ADAM) & TPG RE Finance Trust (NYSE:TRTX)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/head-to-head-contrast-adamas-trust-nasdaqadam-tpg-re-finance-trust-nysetrtx.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793801695.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.954,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Adamas (ADAM) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/arti